; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Koch Snowflake and Anti-Snowflake
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, Koch curve, snowflake, FILLED, island
; SUMMARY:  Paints two Koch islands: a snowflake with bumps out and an anti-snowflake with bumps in.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Walks around a triangle three times with a Koch curve on every
;   side. On the left the bumps point outward and make the famous
;   snowflake. On the right the very same curve is walked the other
;   way round, so the bumps point inward and bite holes into it.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change LEVEL near the bottom to 2, 3 or 5.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * one recursive procedure used in two different ways
;   * how the direction you walk around a shape decides where the
;     bumps go
;   * FILLED painting the inside of a long, wiggly outline
;   * using variables so two drawings stay the same size
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use level 1 for both. Can you see a Star of David on the left?
;   * Make the snowflake twice as wide.
;   * Count the edges: level n has 3 times 4 to the power n of them.
; ============================================================

; SIDE is a Koch curve. The bump always goes to the LEFT of the way
; the turtle is walking.
to side :len :level
  if :level = 0 [forward :len stop]
  side :len / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  side :len / 3 :level - 1
  right 120
  side :len / 3 :level - 1
  left 60
  side :len / 3 :level - 1
end

; ISLAND walks a triangle of Koch curves centered on (x, y).
; :turn is 120 to walk clockwise or -120 to walk counterclockwise.
; Walking clockwise, the inside is on the right, so left bumps poke
; out. Walking counterclockwise, the inside is on the left, so the
; same bumps poke in.
to island :x :y :len :level :turn :color
  ; The triangle's top edge sits a third of its height above the
  ; middle, which is what keeps the whole island centered.
  localmake "h :len * 0.866
  penup setxy :x - :len / 2 :y + :h / 3
  ifelse :turn > 0 [setheading 90] [
    ; going the other way round, start at the right hand corner
    setx :x + :len / 2
    setheading 270
  ]
  pendown
  filled :color [repeat 3 [side :len :level right :turn]]
end

; CAPTION writes a line of text roughly centered at (x, y).
to caption :x :y :text
  penup setxy :x - 4 * count :text :y pendown
  label :text
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 30 60]
make "level 4
setpensize 1.5
setpencolor 7
island -190 10 260 :level 120 [140 200 255]
island 190 10 260 :level -120 [255 190 120]
setlabelheight 16
caption -190 -200 "snowflake
caption 190 -200 "anti-snowflake
